        "titolo_orig": "Cuba’s president warns US against attacking island or trying to depose him",
        "testo_it": "Cuba: il presidente Diaz-Canel avverte gli USA contro tentativi di invasione o deposizione.",
        "priorita": "Media",
        "id_gruppo": 0,
        "link": "https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3349817/cubas-president-warns-us-against-attacking-island-or-trying-depose-him?utm_source=rss_feed",
        "orario": "18:47",
        "timestamp": 1776012420,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement Americas and the Caribbean World Americas Cuba’s president warns US against attacking island or trying to depose him Miguel Diaz-Canel said an invasion of Cuba would be costly and affect regional security but should it happen, Cubans would defend themselves 2 -MIN READ 2 -MIN Listen Associated Press Published: 12:47am, 13 Apr 2026 Updated: 2:11am, 13 Apr 2026 Cuban President Miguel Diaz-Canel said the United States has no valid reason to carry out a military attack against the island or to attempt to depose him. Speaking in an interview on NBC News’ Meet the Press programme, the president said an invasion of Cuba would be costly and affect regional security. But should it happen, Diaz-Canel said, Cubans would defend themselves. “If the time comes, I don’t think there would be any justification for the United States to launch a military aggression against Cuba, or for the US to undertake a surgical operation or the kidnapping of a president,” Diaz-Canel said, speaking through a translator. Advertisement He added: “If that happens, there will be fighting, and there will be a struggle, and we will defend ourselves, and if we need to die, we’ll die, because as our national anthem says, ‘Dying for the homeland is to live.’” His comments come as tensions between Cuba and the US remain high despite both sides acknowledging talks, although no details have been shared. Advertisement Diaz-Canel has accused the US government of implementing a “hostile policy” against Cuba and said it has “no moral to demand anything from Cuba”. He noted that Cuba is interested in engaging in dialogue and discussing any topic without conditions, “not demanding changes from our political system as we are not demanding change from the American system, about which we have a number of doubts”. Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
